{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["The discerning will understand that all the words of our Rabbis and their derashot are valid and true. And this is what is said in the tractate Shabbat (63a): I was eighteen years old, and I did not know that no verse leaves the hand of its plain sense. And the core of the halakhot and the derashot emerge from the superfluity of the verses or from a change of language: the plain sense of a verse was written in language from which the core of the derashah can be derived — as in ״אֵלֶּה תוֹלְדוֹת הַשָּׁמַיִם וְהָאָרֶץ בְּהִבָּרְאָם״, which the Sages derived as ״באברהם״, from the elongation of the language, since there was no need to write ״בְּהִבָּרְאָם״. Now I shall set out the earlier interpretations of this verse, to make known to people why I have not seen fit to explain as they did. There are those who explain: At first Elohim created the heavens and the earth. It is impossible to say thus, for the waters preceded, as it is written: ״וְרוּחַ אֱלֹהִים מְרַחֶפֶת עַל פְּנֵי הַמָּיִם״ (v. 2). Moreover, it is not written here ״בראשונה״ but ״בְּרֵאשִׁית״ — it is in construct state, like ״וַתְּהִי רֵאשִׁית מַמְלַכְתּוֹ בָּבֶל״ (Genesis 10:10). And the one who explains it like ״תְּחִלַּת דִּבֶּר ה׳ בְּהוֹשֵׁעַ״ (Hosea 1:2), meaning: at the beginning of Elohim's creating the heavens, meaning: before He created heavens and earth — הָאָרֶץ הָיְתָה תֹהוּ וָבֹהוּ וְחֹשֶׁךְ עַל פְּנֵי תְהוֹם וְרוּחַ אֱלֹהִים מְרַחֶפֶת עַל פְּנֵי הַמָּיִם, so it turns out that the waters were created first — this too is nothing, for then he should not have written ״וְהָאָרֶץ הָיְתָה תֹהוּ וָבֹהוּ״, since if it had not yet been created, he should not have called it 'eretz' before the creation of the waters, given that the waters preceded. Rather, this is the core of its plain sense according to the way of Scripture, which regularly anticipates and explains a thing not needed for its own context but for something referred to elsewhere — as it is written: ״שֵׁם וְחָם וָיָפֶת״ (Genesis 9:18), and it is written: ״וְחָם הוּא אֲבִי כְנָעַן״ (ibid.). Only because it is written before it ״אָרוּר כְּנָעַן״ — had it not been explained first who Canaan was, we would not have known why Noah cursed him. ״וַיִּשְׁכַּב אֶת בִּלְהָה פִּילֶגֶשׁ אָבִיו וַיִּשְׁמַע יִשְׂרָאֵל״ (Genesis 35:22). Why is ״וַיִּשְׁמַע יִשְׂרָאֵל״ written here? For nothing is written here that Jacob said anything about Reuben! Rather, because at the time of his passing he said: ״פַּחַז כַּמַּיִם אַל תּוֹתַר כִּי עָלִיתָ מִשְׁכְּבֵי אָבִיךָ אָז חִלַּלְתָּ יְצוּעִי עָלָה״ (Genesis 49:4), therefore he anticipated with ״וַיִּשְׁמַע יִשְׂרָאֵל״, so that you not wonder when you see that he rebuked him for this at the end of his days. And so in several places. Also this entire section of the work of the six days, Moshe Rabbenu anticipated and explained for you what the Holy One, blessed be He, said at the hour of the giving of the Torah: ״זָכוֹר אֶת־יוֹם הַשַּׁבָּת לְקַדְּשׁוֹ... כִּי שֵׁשֶׁת יָמִים עָשָׂה יהוה אֶת הַשָּׁמַיִם וְאֶת הָאָרֶץ אֶת הַיָּם וְאֶת כָּל אֲשֶׁר בָּם וַיָּנַח בַּיּוֹם הַשְּׁבִיעִי״ (Exodus 20:7–10). And this is what is written: ״וַיְהִי בֹקֶר יוֹם הַשִּׁשִּׁי״ (v. 31) — that sixth day, which is the completion of the six days that the Holy One, blessed be He, spoke of at the giving of the Torah. Therefore Moshe said to Israel, to inform them that the word of the Holy One, blessed be He, is true: Do you suppose that this world has been all the days as built as you now see it, full of all good? It was not so; rather, ״בְּרֵאשִׁית בָּרָא אֱלֹהִים״ etc., meaning: at the beginning of the creation of heaven and earth, meaning: at the time that the upper heavens and the earth were already created — whether a long time or a short time — then ״וְהָאָרֶץ הָיְתָה״ etc. (v. 2)."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "Rashbam cites Exodus 20:7–10 by chapter and verse; the versification follows the Jewish enumeration where the Decalogue begins at 20:2, making the Sabbath commandment fall at verses 7–10."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T23:16:15.279931898Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}